{
  "title": { "en": "A contradiction, so not" },
  "tray": "proof",
  "intro": [
    {
      "t": {
        "en": "If rain makes the ground wet and also makes it not wet, it cannot be raining."
      }
    }
  ],
  "after": {
    "en": "The other way, from “¬¬it rains” to “it rains”, is beyond these rules."
  },
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "notI_1",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "A contradiction, so not" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "A → B", "q": "A → ¬B" }, "goal": "¬A" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "Rain", "B": "Wet" }, { "A": "Exam", "B": "Study" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "“¬it rains” is “it rains → ⊥”: assume “it rains” and reach ⊥ inside the box."
        }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "f = impI[A=A](body: m3) {",
        "  body {",
        "    m1 = mp(p, f.body)",
        "    m2 = mp(q, f.body)",
        "    m3 = mp(m2, m1)",
        "  }",
        "}",
        "goal <- f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "notI_2",
      "kind": "proof",
      "step": { "en": "It cannot be not" },
      "tests": [{ "premises": { "p": "A" }, "goal": "¬¬A" }],
      "cases": [{ "A": "Rain" }, { "A": "Locked" }],
      "hint": [
        {
          "en": "“¬¬it rains” is “¬it rains → ⊥”. Assume “¬it rains”; it clashes with the given."
        }
      ],
      "intro": [{ "t": { "en": "It is raining, so “it is not raining” cannot hold." } }],
      "solution": ["f = impI[A=\"~A\"](body: m) {", "  body {", "    m = mp(f.body, p)", "  }", "}", "goal <- f"]
    }
  ]
}
